## Proposed Changes

### Backend: Persistent Caches & Auto-Rehydration

#### [NEW] [transcript_cache.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/transcript_cache.py)
- Disk cache for full earnings call transcripts under `backend/transcript_cache/{TICKER}_{year}Q{quarter}.json`.
- Functions:
  - `get_transcript(ticker: str, year: int, quarter: int) -> dict | None`
  - `save_transcript(ticker: str, year: int, quarter: int, doc: TranscriptDoc) -> None`
  - `list_cached_quarters(ticker: str) -> list[str]`

#### [MODIFY] [news_provider.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/providers/news_provider.py)
- In `search_earnings_transcript()`:
  - Check `transcript_cache.get_transcript(ticker, year, quarter)` first.
  - If found, return instantly without calling Tavily.
  - If not found, run Tavily search; upon success, save to `transcript_cache`.

#### [MODIFY] [filing_cache.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/filing_cache.py)
- Add `list_cached_tickers() -> list[str]` to discover all companies with saved filings on disk.
- Ensure `rehydrate_company_store()` robustly restores `text_store`, `table_store`, `filing_meta`, and `metrics_store` and calls `rebuild_merged_tables()`.

#### [MODIFY] [company_service.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/company_service.py)
- In `list_companies(store: DocumentStore)`:
  - Auto-discover tickers from `filing_cache.list_cached_tickers()`.
  - If any cached ticker is not yet in `store`, automatically call `filing_cache.rehydrate_company_store(tk, store)` so `store` is repopulated immediately on startup.

#### [MODIFY] [document.py (router)](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/routers/document.py)
- In `_company_or_404(store, ticker)`:
  - If `not store.has_company(ticker)`: attempt `filing_cache.rehydrate_company_store(ticker, store)` before raising 404.
- In `list_periods(ticker, store)`:
  - If `not store.has_company(ticker)`: attempt `filing_cache.rehydrate_company_store(ticker, store)`.

#### [MODIFY] [history_store.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/rag/history_store.py)
- In `save_analysis()`:
  - Add `agent_contexts: dict | None = None` parameter.
  - Persist `agent_contexts` into the JSON record on disk so raw transcripts and evidence are preserved alongside reports.
- In `get_latest_analysis(ticker: str) -> dict | None`:
  - Ensure fast retrieval of the newest record for any ticker.

#### [MODIFY] [pipeline.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/pipeline.py)
- When saving analysis at the end of the pipeline:
  - Pass `agent_contexts=agent_contexts` to `history_store.save_analysis()`.

#### [MODIFY] [chat.py (router)](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/routers/chat.py)
- In `_agent_chat_persona(agent_id, debate_store, ticker)`:
  - If `debate_store.get(ticker)` is None:
    - Load latest analysis via `history_store.get_latest_analysis(ticker)`.
    - If found, populate `debate` context and cache back to `debate_store.replace(ticker, ...)`.
  - **Eliminates the 409 `"No analysis has been run for '{ticker}' yet"` error** when historical analysis exists on disk!
- In `_coach_chat_persona()`:
  - If `debate_store.get(ticker)` is None, load SEC/technical reports from `history_store.get_latest_analysis(ticker)`.

#### [MODIFY] [research_copilot.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/research_copilot.py)
- In `_earnings_text(debate_store, ticker)`:
  - Check in-memory `debate_store`.
  - Fallback to `history_store.get_latest_analysis(ticker)` (reads `agent_contexts.earnings_call.raw_data` or `reports.earnings_call`).
  - Fallback to `transcript_cache`.
  - Returns grounded earnings-call text even after server restarts.
- In `_financials_text()` and `_sec_text()`:
  - If `store` is empty, auto-rehydrate via `filing_cache.rehydrate_company_store(ticker, store)`.

